Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhen the base-$b$ number $11011_b$ is multiplied by $b-1$, then $1001_b$ is added, what is the result (written in base $b$)?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"aca01f4e623b60268e88f44ffdbc0976551e615016d5e2a912e5189883b66bbf"},"seconds":32.713037967681885,"seed":581265476554269757,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base-$b$ numbers to base-10.\n2. Perform the arithmetic operations in base-10.\n3. Convert the result back to base-$b$.\n\n### Step 1: Convert the base-$b$ numbers to base-10.\n\nThe base-$b$ number $11011_b$ can be converted to base-10 as follows:\n\\[\n11011_b = 1 \\cdot b^4 + 1 \\cdot b^3 + 0 \\cdot b^2 + 1 \\cdot b + 1 = b^4 + b^3 + b + 1\n\\]\n\nThe base-$b$ number $1001_b$ can be converted to base-10 as follows:\n\\[\n1001_b = 1 \\cdot b^3 + 0 \\cdot b^2 + 0 \\cdot b + 1 = b^3 + 1\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Perform the arithmetic operations in base-10.\n\nFirst, multiply $11011_b$ (which is $b^4 + b^3 + b + 1$ in base-10) by $b-1$:\n\\[\n(b^4 + b^3 + b + 1)(b-1) = b^5 + b^4 + b^2 + b - b^4 - b^3 - b - 1 = b^5 - b^3 + b^2 - 1\n\\]\n\nNext, add $1001_b$ (which is $b^3 + 1$ in base-10) to the result:\n\\[\nb^5 - b^3 + b^2 - 1 + b^3 + 1 = b^5 + b^2\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Convert the result back to base-$b$.\n\nThe result in base-10 is $b^5 + b^2$. To convert this back to base-$b$, we write it as:\n\\[\nb^5 + b^2 = 1 \\cdot b^5 + 0 \\cdot b^4 + 0 \\cdot b^3 + 1 \\cdot b^2 + 0 \\cdot b + 0 = 100100_b\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{100100_b}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{100100_b}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
